<title>BRAZIL: RESEARCH ALERT-Telebras estimates raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Telebras estimates raised.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caspian Securities said it has raised its year-end 1998 price target for Brazil's federally-owned telecom giant Telebras to $200 per American Depositary Share (ADS).</p>
<p>-- Caspian analysts Joanne Showalter and Tony Figueiredo also raised their 1997 and 1998 earnings estimate for Telebras to $12.60 and $17.20 per ADS from $11.65 and $16.20, respectively.</p>
<p>-- They also reiterated their buy rating on the company's shares.</p>
</text>
